From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: a calibration file in place comes before nvmem

LOCAL (openwrt-arista, not for upstream): the Arista C-360's dual 5 GHz
radio plan gives the IPQ8074 the calibration data at ART 0x71800, where
the device tree's nvmem cell names 0x1000 (the 6 GHz plan, Arista's
default). The plan writes cal-ahb-c000000.wifi.bin; with no such file the
nvmem cell is used as before. request_firmware_direct: no hotplug wait.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/qmi.c
@@ -2466,6 +2466,7 @@ static int ath11k_qmi_load_bdf_qmi(struc
 {
 	struct device *dev = ab->dev;
 	char filename[ATH11K_QMI_MAX_BDF_FILE_NAME_SIZE];
+	char path[100];
 	struct ath11k_board_data bd;
 	u32 fw_size, file_type;
 	const struct firmware *fw_entry = NULL;
@@ -2513,6 +2514,21 @@ static int ath11k_qmi_load_bdf_qmi(struc
 		fw_size = ATH11K_QMI_MAX_BDF_FILE_NAME_SIZE;
 	} else {
 		file_type = ATH11K_QMI_FILE_TYPE_CALDATA;
+
+		/* A calibration file in place comes before the nvmem cell:
+		 * one a board's radio plan writes, for calibration data the
+		 * device tree does not name.
+		 */
+		snprintf(filename, sizeof(filename), "cal-%s-%s.bin",
+			 ath11k_bus_str(ab->hif.bus), dev_name(dev));
+		ath11k_core_create_firmware_path(ab, filename, path, sizeof(path));
+		if (!request_firmware_direct(&fw_entry, path, dev)) {
+			ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_QMI,
+				   "calibration data from %s before nvmem\n", path);
+			goto success;
+		}
+		fw_entry = NULL;
+
 		ret = ath11k_qmi_get_caldata_nvmem(ab, &caldata, &fw_size);
 		if (!ret) {
 			tmp = caldata;
